so microsoft is expected to acquire  activision for a ton of money and if the  deal goes through microsoft will become  the adoptive parents to loads of massive  franchises but that also means microsoft  is acquiring activision's 43-year legacy  and with it some legendary and not so  legendary ips they've picked up along  the way in a lot of ways microsoft  buying activision is like moving into a  house and finding all the weird [ __ ] the  old tenets left behind in the attic and  it appears the xbox daddy x phil spencer  is ready to find what's between the sofa  cushions really phil spencer told the  washington post that he's eager to  revive some of activision's old games  and let's all hope that it's not loser  suit larry so let's pull some of those  boxes out from activision's musty old  basement and take a look at the  abandoned franchises microsoft now  potentially owns  first we're going to blow the dust off  sierra entertainment cyril were giants  in this industry formed the same year as  activision back in 1979 founders ken and  roberta williams were pioneers in the  interactive medium responsible for the  first graphic adventure game mystery  house what followed was a series of  games that influenced the entire medium  games like king's quest space quest  police quest quest for glory leisure  suit larry gabriel knight and most  importantly the gold mine that microsoft  now sits upon  fan taz magoria  [Music]  phantasmagoria was roberta williams's  magnum opus for years roberta had wanted  to make a horror game but held off until  the technology was there to tell the  story how she had always envisioned it  it wasn't until cd-roms became faster  and could handle real actors that she  decided to go all in on her first horror  escapade in horror it certainly was  phantasmagoria is about a woman who  moves into a remote mansion with her  husband but is soon tormented by  supernatural forces that rip her world  and marriage apart it's dark extremely  graphic and takes many liberties to  convey its horror a radical contrast to  roberta's previous rather light-hearted  adventures when it was released in 1995  it garnered a lot of controversy for its  depiction of adult themes and violence  nor did sierra entertainment shy away  from owning it  phantasmagoria's true legacy is in  taking a daring step in using the medium  as well as cutting-edge technology at  the time to tell a powerful and  horrifying story seldom seen in games  all that said microsoft has a potential  revival for a horror franchise here or  you know they could just put it on game  pass or something at least it's sequel  however  uh well that's a box that might want to  stay in the activision attic  tucked under the stairs is raven's  software's family photo album raven most  commonly known today as being a support  studio for call of duty came from a  lineage of classic first-person shooters  like heretic or the hyper-violent  soldiers of fortune and the badass dark  fantasy rpg hexen  while microsoft now owns the mighty  fantasy elder scrolls series hexen falls  more into the doom category of action  and the potential to revive it with that  dna could be sweet to see it's also just  kind of cool to see that raven and id  software are now roomies again but then  their singularity raven's last big  outing before shifting over to being a  call of duty support studio singularity  attempted to be a lot of things with  inspirations and mechanics ranging from  fear bioshock and half-life 2 it mixed  special abilities with first person  shooting with a sprinkle of horror its  use of combining special powers into the  shooter genre was also an idea raven  software explored in their rather  bemused take on wolfenstein in 2009  which also gave bj blaskowitz  supernatural abilities and  black hair  but unlike wolfenstein the mashing of  concepts shined in singularity it's  something of a lost gem for 2010  shooters one that xbox may want to  examine for its potential in the future  now i know radical entertainment for  jackie chan stunt master  but i'm willing to bet most of you  probably know them for prototype  prototype was an accumulation of  radical's best efforts like the  incredible hulk ultimate destruction put  into an original ip setting the player  loose in an open world sandbox using  slick traversal and over-the-top  superpowers  radical entertainment was made a support  team for destiny but now that sony is  set to acquire bungie it's unclear what  radical is working on next under the  activision roof look even if microsoft  doesn't give them the chance to make the  once canceled prototype 3 they should  try to work out a sweet deal with marvel  to get another hulk ultimate destruction  underway as for jack a chance to  unmaster leave it alone it's a gem and  it's perfect exactly how it is  i'm sure neversoft has its own room in  the activision abode one that has tony  hawk and guitar hero memorabilia  everywhere and a little statue to  commemorate gun but if phil decided to  look under the carpet i'm sure he'd find  apocalypse the action shooter starring  bruce willis  now if i'm being completely honest i  don't see a future in which this exists  but i deemed it appropriate to live here  in this video as i did not know about  its existence since beginning my  research now i feel somehow compelled to  play it only to hear bruce willis  screams suck on this  while system of the down concerts play  on giant screens amidst exploding  buildings  it's a thing  and of course there's the legacy  activision has with its very own ips  that help kick this entire industry off  like pitfall  [Music]  sure there's uncharted and tomb raider  but now microsoft has its own  adventurous ip to swing and traverse the  eclectic jungles of the world i mean  but uh then again machine games is  working on an indiana jones game which  microsoft now also owns uh  whatever anyways let's not forget about  the true crime series yes sleeping 